      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b52ba672b29a515be8ff219|full_name}: I don't know what websites you're using, but on almost all of the social sites I use (Reddit, Discord, Twitter, Gmail, Youtube, Twitch) I didn't have to provide more than a name and an email address, and it didn't even have to be my real name. \n\nOccasionally a site will ask for more information, but generally it's not required, and generally you can hide as much of your personal information from your profile as you want. \n\nFor example I cannot even click on your name to view your profile here, but even if I could, I know that it wouldn't tell me much because you're using a fake name and they didn't ask for my age or location on sign up, only an email address. And generally even when your profile is visible a site will hide your email address to prevent spam, so that wouldn't be visible regardless. \n\nThe only social media site I've signed up for which I've provided my age, name, gender, and location for is Facebook. I may have provided my age to Steam and the Oculus store. But it's not like they bother to verify it. And it's not displayed in my profile for people to see. Even Facebook doesn't tell people how old you are! And any sites which do list where you're from, like some forums I post on, that information is either entirely optional to provide, or you can simply lie about it, and change it at any time to suit your whims.\n\n> Why don't you want it to be in VRChat too? \n\nBecause even though I personally have no interest in pretending to be a girl online, I have a few friends in the trans community and I don't want to enable people like you to discriminate against them. Is that clear enough for you?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
