      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": "5c7725d506f5ca513a40fd29",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "One of the reasons many VRChat users find interaction in VR so fascinating is that you don't have to be defined by how you look in real life. Forcing users to label themselves or conform to restrictive social norms only serves to hinder the spirit of free expression and progression as a community. Of course, it's perfectly fine to have your views on such topics (and to debate them respectfully in private), and there is absolutely nothing stopping users from putting gender symbols in their names, on avatars, or in their status messages. Users who do not want to disclose personally identifying factors will not be forced to do so.\n\nThis suggestion is being closed for this reason, among others. \n\nWe encourage you to take a look at our Community Guidelines, in particular the section prohibiting intolerance:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/community\n\n[VRChat prohibits] Discrimination towards spiritual beliefs, gender, sexual orientation, sexual identity, disability, and/or any other personally identifying factors.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
